      {
        "id": "audit_title",
        "parent": "1",
        "source": "",
        "target": "",
        "style": "text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=29;align=left;verticalAlign=top;",
        "text": "AUCTION / verification coverage and semantic limits"
      },
      {
        "id": "coverage",
        "parent": "1",
        "source": "",
        "target": "",
        "style": "text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=top;",
        "text": "1 / State supplied by the CSL core   Auction::start(service) reads running and writes running/task. Auction::bid(amount) reads running; an improving bid updates best_bid/currentWinner. A successful losing bid can change no state. Auction::stop() reads running, sets it false and publishes winner.  The five supplied Auction operation pre/post clauses have the required Boolean/String state. Their operation signatures belong to the execution/USE adapter, not CSL structural declarations.  String task represents the service description. winner remains a String encoding the source Atom, including no_winner."
      },
      {
        "id": "external",
        "parent": "1",
        "source": "",
        "target": "",
        "style": "text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=top;",
        "text": "2 / Required external observer state    AuctionMonitor  / SchemeOrder and BidEvidence: startSatisfiedAt, bidEnabledAt, bidSatisfiedAt, decideEnabledAt, decideSatisfiedAt, now; bidCommittedBy, bidDoneBy, actualBidBy; adminBidOverride.   AuctionObligation  / WithinDeadline: goal, activatedAt, deadlineAt, endedAt, unfulfilled, monitor.  These are event/deontic trace projections. They are deliberately not Entity classes or an Association in CSL core. Role players are not the same set as mission-committed bidders. step.enabled / step.succeeded and agent-artifact focus also remain runtime evidence. The supplied OCL contains no @pre.  No Auction snapshot can prove a non-improving actual bid occurred, or reconstruct the 10 s / 1 h obligation history."
      },
      {
        "id": "decisions",
        "parent": "1",
        "source": "",
        "target": "",
        "style": "text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=top;",
        "text": "3 / KEEP, MODIFY, REMOVE, ADD    KEEP:  auctionGroup, auctioneer, participant, Auction, id and the four observable properties.  MODIFY:  CSL notation; types, mutability and identifier origin; separate role-population bounds from declaration containment.  REMOVE:  Bid with amount/bidderName; opens-closes, submits, offers, and the untyped auction-sessions association.  ADD:  root AuctionOrg, explicit OrgCtx declaration nesting, persistent source field currentWinner, source population Phi.  No Service Entity: source stores only a String. No winner-to-Role association: source stores an agent-name Atom. No subgroup, Role inheritance, Compatibility, or Role-to-Role Link is declared by this case study. No Goal/Mission/Norm is a CSL node."
      },
      {
        "id": "integration",
        "parent": "1",
        "source": "",
        "target": "",
        "style": "text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;",
        "text": "4 / Integration limits verified in use4Goal   The v4 grammar/compiler supports structural parse, reference validation, and scalar attributes. It declares no operations.  CslModel.requireLegacyRuntime rejects a v4 model in the legacy CSL-to-USE/runtime backend. A valid CSL diagram is not evidence of a completed executable bridge.  The iStar organization Actor Auction needs an explicit context correspondence. A direct OrgCtx mapping does not by itself satisfy the paper's total Actor-to-Role rule in Definition 4(iii). No artificial coordinator Role is introduced to hide that gap.  Binding each Task to Auction.id and its invocation is required for concurrent a1/a2; self:Auction is not automatically the paper's shared self:c:OrgCtx convention."
      },
      {
        "id": "source_trace",
        "parent": "1",
        "source": "",
        "target": "",
        "style": "text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;",
        "text": "5 / Source and notation evidence   Mandatory local Auction folder: auction.jcm:8-31; src/org/auction-os.xml:14-50. src/agt/auction_capabilities.asl:2-13,19-42,53-57. src/env/auction_env/AuctionArtifact.java:8-44.  Paper: IV-A/IV-C, Fig. 6-7 and ProposalReview (pages 2-4). use4Goal: docs/model/csl.ecore; CSL.g4; CslBuildingVisitor; CslModelFactory; CslSemanticValidator; CslLayoutBuilder; CslUseViewModel; CslModel.requireLegacyRuntime.  ProposalReview records persistent revisions/reviews/validations. Auction has no corresponding stored Bid record; no such Entity or action-derived structural Association is copied mechanically."
      },
      {
        "id": "numeric_identity",
        "parent": "1",
        "source": "",
        "target": "",
        "style": "text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;",
        "text": "6 / Explicit abstractions and observation limits   id projects CArtAgO artifact-name metadata via scheme Id. AuctionOrg is model scope, not physical workspace containment. currentWinner exists in Java but is not observable; extracting it requires explicit access/instrumentation. The current OCL does not read it; it records the candidate-to-published-winner semantics. Java double / Atom are projected to USE Real / String. Preserve Double.MAX_VALUE, or declare a justified finite-domain abstraction separately. No zero/default or artificial Bid history is substituted."
      },
      {
        "id": "audit_footer",
        "parent": "1",
        "source": "",
        "target": "",
        "style": "text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=top;",
        "text": "Coverage verdict:  organizational declarations and source domain state are represented. Domain operation guards/effects can use Auction state. Full goal/task/deadline verification still requires explicit correspondences, execution evidence and the v4 runtime adapter; observer helpers are not part of this CSL model."
      }
    ]
  },
