      {
        "id": "notes_title",
        "parent": "1",
        "source": "",
        "target": "",
        "style": "text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=29;align=left;verticalAlign=top;",
        "text": "AUCTION / semantic contract and source trace"
      },
      {
        "id": "ownership",
        "parent": "1",
        "source": "",
        "target": "",
        "style": "text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=top;",
        "text": "1 / Goal reliance and actor association   auction = AND(start, bid, decide), all within Auction. mAuctioneer = {start, decide}; mParticipant = {bid}. participates-in describes Role-to-Organization association only. Three Goal Dependencies express who is expected to achieve the goals. Each has an external dependum and two directed D-marked legs. Auction's child goals are depender elements; they have no refinements of their own. Role-side dependee goals may be refined into Tasks. Dependency failure is possible and does not make the notation invalid."
      },
      {
        "id": "plans",
        "parent": "1",
        "source": "",
        "target": "",
        "style": "text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=top;",
        "text": "2 / Jason task mapping    start : makeArtifact; focus; start(Service). ASL 19-25.  decide : ?focusing(...); stop. ASL 27-30. The query retrieves the existing focus; it does not refocus.  bid : lookupArtifact; focus; if random < 0.9, wait and bid; otherwise .fail. ASL 32-42. The code says 0.9; its 80% comment is stale.  org-obedient.asl calls goalAchieved only after !Goal succeeds. A successful bid need not improve best_bid or become winner. AuctionArtifact.stop publishes currentWinner, including no_winner.  The AND task refinements show the necessary successful plan steps. The .fail branch is not modeled as an alternative achievement."
      },
      {
        "id": "conditions",
        "parent": "1",
        "source": "",
        "target": "",
        "style": "text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=top;",
        "text": "3 / Thesis extended iStar: evaluating the goals   Section IV-A / Fig. 4 / Table I: refinement and dependency values are propagated; leaf Conditions bind execution to the shared state.  The organizational children now obtain achievement via dependencies. They are not additionally assigned self.*SatisfiedAt >= 0 conditions. A MOISE administrative state must not override a failed actual-bid dependency in the goal model.  Setup/query leaf Tasks: pre = step.enabled; post = step.succeeded. Artifact-call Tasks: source operation contracts plus observed success. step is keyed by scheme run, role player and invocation. Goals use Achieve within one run; MOISE performance is a separate type. A successful protocol run need not achieve every normative iStar goal."
      },
      {
        "id": "monitor",
        "parent": "1",
        "source": "",
        "target": "",
        "style": "text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=top;",
        "text": "4 / Explicit observer interface for the OCL   AuctionMonitor is a required trace projection, not a Java source class. One instance per scheme run / auction Id. Integer times are in ms on one clock; -1 means the event has not occurred.   now startSatisfiedAt, bidEnabledAt, bidSatisfiedAt decideEnabledAt, decideSatisfiedAt : Integer bidCommittedBy, bidDoneBy, actualBidBy : Set(String) adminBidOverride : Boolean   Satisfied/enabled times come from MOISE, not artifact return times. bidDoneBy comes from done(Sch,bid,Ag); actualBidBy from successful bid calls, including non-winning bids. Do not infer either from winner. bidCommittedBy is frozen at the first bid satisfaction (current before it). adminBidOverride records only an observed successful admin command. These fields audit scheme status; they do not define normative goal values."
      },
      {
        "id": "deadlines",
        "parent": "1",
        "source": "",
        "target": "",
        "style": "text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=18;align=left;verticalAlign=top;",
        "text": "5 / Deadline and recovery semantics   bid: ttf = 10000 ms. decide: ttf = 3600000 ms. OS 34-35. Use each obligation's activation/deadline from MOISE, including a later mission commitment; do not time from MAS startup.  AuctionObligation: one record per bid/decide obligation activation.  goal : String  -- bid or decide activatedAt, deadlineAt, endedAt : Integer unfulfilled : Boolean; monitor : AuctionMonitor  endedAt = first terminal engine time (fulfilled/unfulfilled/inactive), or -1 while pending. Use engine times, not notification receipt times. unfulfilled remains true after oblUnfulfilled; never erase the record.  WithinDeadline is a conformance norm: pending overtime also fails. Admin recovery allows progress but does not repair an expired duty. Thus the scheme can finish while the iStar bidding goal is unachieved."
      },
      {
        "id": "sources",
        "parent": "1",
        "source": "",
        "target": "",
        "style": "text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;",
        "text": "6 / Verified references and scope   Local JaCaMo examples/auction: src/org/auction-os.xml: 14-24, 28-50. src/agt/auction_capabilities.asl: 19-42, 53-57. src/env/auction_env/AuctionArtifact.java: 18-44. Resolved moise-1.1.jar: asl/org-obedient.asl; Scheme.isSatisfied and SchemeBoard.admCommand.   iStar 2.0 Language Guide : sections 2, 3, 5, 6.1, 6.2, 8. Supplied thesis PDF: section IV-A, Fig. 4, Table I (page 3).  ASL 53-57 handles oblUnfulfilled with goalSatisfied(bid). No blacklist task is added: the source contains only a TODO. Bid Dependency is instantiated per committed Participant enactment; normal global completion requires all such agents, not one winning bid."
      },
      {
        "id": "notes_footer",
        "parent": "1",
        "source": "",
        "target": "",
        "style": "text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=17;align=left;verticalAlign=top;",
        "text": "Standard iStar has no generic Goal-to-Goal Association. Cross-actor reliance uses Dependency; mission trace annotations are not semantic edges. The unchanged OCL audits sequence, evidence and deadlines, including administrative recovery; it does not erase normative dependency failure."
      }
    ]
  },
